    <statement><p>Calculate <m>\mathbf{r}'(t)</m>, <m>\mathbf{T}(t)</m>, and <m>\mathbf{T}(2)</m> where
<me>\mathbf{r}(t)=\langle t^{4}, t^{3}\rangle.</me></p>
<p><m>\mathbf{r}'(t) = \langle</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/><m>,</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/><m>\rangle</m>.</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{T}(t) = \langle</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/><m>,</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/><m>\rangle</m>.</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{T}(2) = \langle</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/><m>,</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0006"/><m>\rangle</m>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4t^{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3t^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{4t^{3}}{\sqrt{\left(4t^{3}\right)^{2}+\left(3t^{2}\right)^{2}}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{3t^{2}}{\sqrt{\left(4t^{3}\right)^{2}+\left(3t^{2}\right)^{2}}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.936329</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.351123</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\mathbf{r}(t)</m> to obtain:
<me>\mathbf{r}'(t)=\langle 4t^{3},3t^{2} \rangle</me>
and so
<me>||\mathbf{r}'(t)||=\sqrt{\left(4t^{3}\right)^{2}+\left(3t^{2}\right)^{2}}.</me>
We now find the unit tangent vector:
<me>\mathbf{T}(t)
=\frac{\mathbf{r}'(t)}{||\mathbf{r}'(t)||}
=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\left(4t^{3}\right)^{2}+\left(3t^{2}\right)^{2}}}\langle 4t^{3}, 3t^{2} \rangle.</me>
For <m>t=2</m> we obtain the vector:
<me>\mathbf{T}(2)
=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1168}}\langle 32,12\rangle
=\left\langle \frac{32}{\sqrt{1168}}, \frac{12}{\sqrt{1168}} \right\rangle.</me>


</solution>
